00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.840
But as you can imagine, a lot going on.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.530
For those of you that
this is the first time

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:07.640
that you're coming to this livestream,

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.010
the whole point of it is we obviously

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:13.360
have these mass school closures going on

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.620
and we, at Khan Academy we find ourselves

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.120
in a somewhat unique
situation of realizing

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.760
that this is what Khan Academy
to some degree was made for

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.160
even though we've never really thought

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.490
of this circumstance actually happening.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:29.520
And this is clearly a very, situation,

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.610
I don't think anyone would want this,

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:32.850
the ideal circumstance is
that the schools are open,

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:37.370
Academy is somehow a substitute
for live experiences.

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:39.400
We've always imagined
them being in partnership

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.310
with incredible teachers and classrooms

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.410
and you have your peers and
you can liberate the classroom

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.610
to then go to higher order tasks.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:47.180
But we've also imagined Khan Academy

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:49.050
being used in parts of the world

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:51.430
where students might not
have access to school

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:53.400
or might not have access to certain,

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:57.060
to instruction or curriculum
material of certain qualities.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.380
And we now find ourselves in a situation

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:03.010
where most of the world
is going to find ourselves

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:08.010
in that second category.

